Description: do not keep deleted thread rows in the removal list
 RemoveProcessItems() deleted every ThreadItem in the first pass but
 left the dangling pointers in the same BList the second pass re-reads;
 casting freed rows worked only because the legacy allocator kept the
 pages mapped, and faults with a segmentation violation on VOS (crash
 trace: MainWindow.cpp:412, dynamic_cast on freed memory). Remove each
 handled entry from the list as it is deleted.
Author: VitruvianOS Packagers <maintainers@v-os.dev>
Forwarded: no
Origin: https://github.com/HaikuArchives/Slayer
--- a/src/MainWindow.cpp
+++ b/src/MainWindow.cpp
@@ -404,6 +404,10 @@ MainWindow::RemoveProcessItems(BList* items)
 				team_item->thread_items_list->del(p1->thread);
 
 			delete p1;
+			// Drop the dangling pointer: the second pass below re-reads
+			// this list, and casting deleted rows faults on VOS (the
+			// legacy allocator used to keep the pages mapped).
+			items->RemoveItem(i--);
 		}
 	}
 
